      <div class="feature-grid">
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="fhead"><span class="ficon">📊</span><h3>Dashboard</h3></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Today's appointment count, revenue, and a next-up preview at a glance</li>
            <li>Quick actions jump straight to booking, prescribing, or taking payment</li>
            <li>View adapts by role — the receptionist's dashboard drops clinical stats entirely</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="fhead"><span class="ficon">👥</span><h3>Patients</h3></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Live search by name or phone across the full patient list</li>
            <li>A detail page consolidates history: appointments, consultations, prescriptions, and billing in one place</li>
            <li>Delete is doctor-only and warns before removing a record</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="fhead"><span class="ficon">📅</span><h3>Appointments</h3></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Bookings grouped by date — newest first — instead of one undifferentiated list</li>
            <li>List and timeline views of the same schedule</li>
            <li>Status moves through Scheduled → In Progress → Completed as the doctor actually works through the day</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="fhead"><span class="ficon">🩺</span><h3>Consultation</h3></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Symptoms, diagnosis, vitals, and notes captured against a patient's full visit history</li>
            <li>Saving a consultation closes the loop — it marks the originating appointment complete automatically</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="fhead"><span class="ficon">💊</span><h3>Prescription</h3></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Doctor builds an itemized prescription — medicine, dosage, frequency, duration — with live preview</li>
            <li>Receptionist gets a read-only, searchable view built for printing at the front desk</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="fhead"><span class="ficon">💳</span><h3>Billing</h3></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Revenue, pending balance, and invoice count surfaced before the transaction table</li>
            <li>Pending payments move to Paid in one click; filters keep the table scannable</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="feature-card">
          <div class="fhead"><span class="ficon">🧑‍⚕️</span><h3>Staff</h3></div>
