        <div class="feature-card wide ai">
          <div class="fhead"><span class="ficon">✨</span><h3>AI Assistant — grounded, not generic</h3></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Detects intent from the question — a patient's name, "pending payments," "revenue," "appointments" — and pulls the matching rows straight from Postgres before calling the model</li>
            <li>No vector database or embeddings: matching is plain substring/regex logic against fields already in the clinic's own tables, which keeps every answer traceable back to a real query</li>
            <li>Every exchange is logged, and every reply carries a visible disclaimer to verify against the record — the assistant is a summary tool, not a clinical decision-maker</li>
          </ul>
