        <div><span class="eyebrow">04 — Field notes</span><h2>A bug worth writing up.</h2></div>
      </div>

      <div class="case">
        <div class="tag2">Full-stack</div>
        <div>
          <h3>"Completed" that never completed</h3>
          <p>The appointments dashboard tracked a Completed count that could never move — clicking Start just navigated to the consultation form and touched nothing else. There was no backend path to change an appointment's status beyond cancelling it.</p>
          <p><span class="fix">Fix:</span> added <code>/start</code> and <code>/complete</code> endpoints, carried the appointment id through the consultation flow via the URL, and closed the loop so saving a consultation marks its appointment done automatically — verified by driving the real UI end-to-end, not just the API in isolation.</p>
        </div>
